## 2026-06-11 — session start: B-4 (discreteness) + B-5 (ZLattice packaging)

Branch: feat/forster-214-discreteness (off origin/main 9289f91).

Design (statement-level, before implementation):

* Engine file `Jacobians/RiemannSurface/PeriodDiscreteness.lean` (axiom-free):
  - `loopPeriodVec x₀ b γ : Fin (genus X) → ℂ` — coordinate period vector of a
    closed analytic loop (`canonicalArcIntegral γ.arc (b i)`).
  - `loopPeriodLattice x₀ b := span ℤ (range (loopPeriodVec x₀ b))` — the
    Forster-model period lattice (ℤ-span of ALL closed-analytic-loop periods;
    no chosen cycle basis, no axiom).
  - `span_real_loopPeriodLattice_eq_top` — B-3 transported into coordinates
    (axiom-free analogue of PeriodSpan's C3).
  - Generic Mathlib glue: `n = finrank ℝ E` vectors that ℝ-span give
    `DiscreteTopology (span ℤ (range v))` + `IsZLattice` via
    `basisOfTopLeSpanOfCardEqFinrank` + the `ZSpan` instances.
  - **Named hypothesis (the honest residual)** `PeriodGeneratingLoops x₀ b γs`:
    a `Fin (2g)`-family of analytic loops whose period vectors ℤ-generate every
    loop's period vector. This is the lattice shadow of "H₁ is generated by 2g
    loop classes" — topological rank-count content (Forster §21.4b), NOT
    Hodge-theoretic; no R1/R2 anywhere.
  - B-4 headline: `discreteTopology_loopPeriodLattice (hgen) :
    DiscreteTopology (loopPeriodLattice x₀ b)` — 2g generators spanning a
    2g-real-dimensional space form an ℝ-basis; ZSpan discreteness.
  - B-5 headlines: `isZLattice_loopPeriodLattice` (needs only B-3 spanning +
    the DiscreteTopology instance, NOT hgen), ℤ-basis existence
    (`Basis.restrictScalars`), `finrank ℤ = 2g`.

* Transport file `Jacobians/Layer3/PeriodLatticeDiscrete.lean` (consumes
  AX_PeriodCycleBasis only through the DEFINITION of
  `loopIntegralToH1`/`periodLatticeInBasis`, and only the
  loops/isBasis/loops_to_basis fields — R1/R2 never touched):
  - `choiceLoops_periodGenerating` — the chosen witness's loops discharge the
    named hypothesis.
  - `loopPeriodLattice_eq_periodLatticeInBasis` — Forster-model lattice =
    official lattice.
  - R2-free re-derivations of `DiscreteTopology (periodLatticeInBasis ...)` and
    `IsZLattice ℝ (periodLatticeInBasis ...)` (same statements as Phase-C's
    Siegel route, new derivation surviving any future R2 removal).

Circularity guard: engine file imports only PeriodNondegeneracy + Mathlib;
